# Fixed defect 580, 2026-10-10 (panel 207 R3; the critic's `s07`): an `assert`
# is a statement, not an integer operator, so `assert 1 == 2` in a constant's
# body is not judged when the program is compiled. It fails where `V` is read,
# the `1` before it flushed first.

constant V: i64
    assert 1 == 2
    5

function main()
    print(1)
    print(V)
